auth {
  mode: inherit
}

docs {
  The operator surface: creating restaurants (docs/DECISIONS.md D14).

  A fourth trust level, and the only one scoped to no restaurant -- it is what creates them.
  Authorised by `X-Platform-Token`, a shared secret from the deployment's environment, not by a
  staff JWT: a staff token carries exactly one `restaurant_id` (D3), so no staff role can
  describe an operator acting across all of them.

  **The group is not mounted unless `TABLEX_PLATFORM_TOKEN` is set.** Without it these requests
  answer **404**, not 401 -- a deployment that does not onboard tenants over HTTP has no
  tenant-creating endpoint at all. Locally the token is in `backend/config/local.yml` and
  mirrored into `platform_token` in the environment.

  Sequenced last on purpose. Onboarding writes a third restaurant, and running it before the
  folders that assert exact counts and statuses against the two seeded ones would make those
  assertions depend on this one having run.
}
